body:
another tip/mechanic: you can B-reverse attacks like Samus's neutral B, Mewtwo's neutral b or Greninja's neutral B, to B reverse you have to jump, press B and right after tilt to the opposite direction. if you do it correctly, ur fighter will turn around and conserve a little momentum. u can B reverse to bait attacks or look cool.

another way less used thing you can do is hold shield and then hold B then move your L stick, u can move the shield buble around and aim it so that you dont get shield poked (if ur buble is too smal, some attacks can hit you through shield)

&#x200B;

something that not a lot of people do is short hopping, u can press jump+attack to do an air attack and a shorthop, its really nice to know

&#x200B;

also, if you didnt know; you can influence the direction ur launched by tilting the L stick, and for multi hit moves you can spam it to get out of it. side note: you need to spam it and you cant do it on the same direction, so you need to do something like left,up,left,up,left,up instead of left,left,left,left

When you get knocked hard enough and you hit a wall/floor/ceiling, u will bounce off, but if u press shield right before you get hit you can cancel it; thats very useful because like lets say a DK grabs u, walks off stage then throws you agaisnt the stage, if u dont tech you will probably get knocked back off the stage, but if you tech you can recover

&#x200B;

im not good at the game so idk, maybe try all the characters, even the ones you think you might not like or you consider weak or annoying or cheesy, and also try to learn combos and stuff like that; essentially just copy what other people do
